messages:    1%|          | 2/204 [00:00<00:11, 17.08it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: B\n', 'To determine whether the statement "James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1. **James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From the context: "All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.".\n   - Therefore, James is instructed by professor David.\n\n2. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - From the context: "All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.".\n   - Therefore, James is taking the database course.\n\n3. **James is not taking the database course.**.\n   - From the previous step, we know James is taking the database course.\n   - This contradicts the information that James is taking the database course.\n\nSince the information provided leads to a contradiction, we cannot definitively determine whether James is taking the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university. .\n\nLet\'s re-evaluate the statement:.\n- If James is not taking the database course, we need to check if he has a part-time job offered by the university.\n- From the context: "All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.".\n- James is working in the lab, not the library.\n- Therefore, James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\nGiven the contradiction in the database course information, we cannot definitively say James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university. Thus, the statement is uncertain. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
