\\lor Q) \\rightarrow (R \\lor S) \\).\n\n### Applying the Given Information:.\n- From the context, we know that all products of Baked by Melissa are cupcakes, and all cupcakes are bakeries. Therefore, any product of Baked by Melissa is a bakery.\n- Since all products of Baked by Melissa are bakeries, and all bakeries are not spicy (from point 1), any product of Baked by Melissa cannot be spicy.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nSince dried Thai chilies cannot be spicy (as they would contradict the fact that all products of Baked by Melissa are not spicy), and since dried Thai chilies cannot be a bakery (as all products of Baked by Melissa are bakeries), the only possibility left is that dried Thai chilies are a hotpot.\n\nTherefore, dried Thai chilies are a hotpot, which means they are not a product of Baked by Melissa.\n\n### Final Answer:.\nThe statement "Dried Thai chilies are not a product of Baked by Melissa" is **True**.\n\nSo, the correct option is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
