messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: B\n', 'Let\'s break down the information step by step to determine if the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain.\n\n### Step-by-Step Analysis:.\n\n1. **No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the library, they are not from the computer science department.\n\n2. **All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This means if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must work in the library.\n\n3. **All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means if a student takes the database course, they are from the computer science department.\n\n4. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This means if a student is instructed by professor David, they are taking the database course.\n\n5. **All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - From point 5, since James works in the lab, he is instructed by professor David.\n\n7. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - Since James is instructed by professor David, he is taking the database course.\n\n8. **All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - Since James is taking the database course, he is from the computer science department.\n\n9. **No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - Since James is from the computer science department, he cannot work in the library.\n\n10. **James is working in the lab.**.\n    - Since James is working in the lab, he cannot work in the library (from point 9).\n\n11. **All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n    - Since James is not working in the library, he does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nBased on the given information, James does not have a part-time job offered by the university. Therefore, the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
