messages:   24%|##3       | 48/204 [00:05<00:17,  8.80it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Tom can apply for financial aid from ETS to take the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: C\n', 'To determine whether the statement "Tom can apply for financial aid from ETS to take the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s break down the information provided and analyze it step by step.\n\n### Context Analysis:\n1. **Cost of GRE Test**: It costs US $205 to take the GRE test.\n2. **Financial Aid Offered by ETS**: ETS provides financial aid to GRE applicants who prove economic hardship.\n3. **Definition of Economic Hardship**: Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources.\n4. **Tom\'s Situation**:\n   - Tom lives in a single-parent family.\n   - His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n### Reasoning:\n1. **Economic Hardship Definition**: Economic hardship is defined as difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources.\n2. **Tom\'s Situation**: Tom\'s dad has been out of work for more than a year. This indicates that Tom\'s family is experiencing financial difficulties, which aligns with the definition of economic hardship.\n3. **ETS Financial Aid Policy**: ETS provides financial aid to applicants who prove economic hardship.\n\nGiven that Tom\'s family is experiencing financial difficulties (his dad has been out of work for more than a year), it is reasonable to conclude that Tom\'s family meets the criteria for economic hardship.\n\n### Conclusion:\nSince Tom\'s family meets the criteria for economic hardship, Tom can apply for financial aid from ETS to take the GRE test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n**A) True**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
