messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: B\n', 'Let\'s break down the information step by step to determine if the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain.\n\n### Step-by-Step Analysis:.\n\n1. **"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given in the context.\n\n2. **If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**.\n   - Since "Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show, Karen will binge-watch "Stranger Things.".\n\n3. **If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**.\n   - Since Karen will binge-watch "Stranger Things," she will download "Stranger Things.".\n\n4. **Karen does not download "Black Mirror."**.\n   - This is given in the context.\n\n5. **"Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.**.\n   - This is given in the context.\n\n6. **If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.**.\n   - Since Karen will binge-watch "Stranger Things," she will share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nBased on the given information, Karen will binge-watch "Stranger Things" because it is a popular Netflix show. Since she will binge-watch "Stranger Things," she will download it, and since she will download it, she will share it to Lisa.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is **true**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
