 rent or more.\n- Since the security deposit must be no more than $1500, it cannot be equal to $2000 (which is more than $1500).\n\n### Step 4: Determine the Security Deposit\n- Given that the security deposit must be no more than $1500, and it cannot be $2000, the security deposit must be $1500.\n\n### Step 5: Evaluate the Conditions for Renting\n- Tom is allowed to move in with Fluffy (since Fluffy is a pet and pets are allowed in some managed buildings).\n- The security deposit at The Olive Garden is $1500, which is no more than $1500.\n\n### Conclusion\nSince both conditions for renting (being allowed to move in with Fluffy and the security deposit being no more than $1500) are met, Tom will rent an apartment in The Olive Garden.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n**A) True**. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
