messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings. If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets. If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age. If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members. If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly. Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Luke complains often about annoying siblings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: C\n', 'To determine whether the statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s break down the information provided step by step:.\n\n1. **Luke either is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.**.\n   - This means Luke\'s situation can be categorized into two mutually exclusive scenarios:.\n     a) Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members.\n     b) Luke is neither a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n2. **If people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.**.\n   - This means if Luke is a twin or triplet, he would spend a lot of time with his siblings.\n\n3. **If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.**.\n   - This means if Luke has siblings who are the same age, he must be a twin or triplet.\n\n4. **If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age.**.\n   - This means if Luke complains often about annoying siblings, he must have siblings who are the same age.\n\n5. **If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members.**.\n   - This means if Luke does not live at home regularly, he would not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\n6. **If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.**.\n   - This means if Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, he often did not live at home regularly.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze Luke\'s situation based on the given information:.\n\n- Luke either is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\nGiven this, we can infer:.\n- If Luke is a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, then he must be spending a lot of time with his siblings (from point 2 and 6).\n- If Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, then he often did not live at home regularly (from point 6).\n- If Luke did not live at home regularly, then he would not develop strong bonds with his family members (from point 5).\n\nThis creates a contradiction because Luke is stated to develop strong bonds with his family members. Therefore, Luke cannot be a twin or triplet and develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\nSince Luke cannot be a twin or triplet and develop strong bonds with his family members, he must be neither a twin or triplet nor develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\nGiven this, Luke does not spend a lot of time with his siblings (since he does not develop strong bonds with them). Therefore, he does not often not live at home regularly (since he does not develop strong bonds with his family members).\n\nSince Luke does not spend a lot of time with his siblings, he does not complain often about annoying siblings (from point 4).\n\nThus, the statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is false. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 67%|######6   | 136/204 [00:11<00:02, 25.06it/s]
