lso know George has access to a program, so he can compose (\\( \\text{Has Access to a Program} \\rightarrow \\text{Can Compose} \\)).\n\n4. **Can George compose?**.\n   - Since George can compose (\\( \\text{Can Compose} \\)), and he wants to compose (\\( \\text{Wants to Compose} \\)), we can use the third condition: \\( \\text{Can Compose} \\land \\text{Wants to Compose} \\rightarrow \\text{Will Compose} \\).\n\nTherefore, based on the given conditions, if George likes music and has access to a program, he will compose.\n\n### Conclusion:.\nThe statement "If George likes music and has access to a program, he will compose" is true. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
